From: dmdhrumilmistry <56185972+dmdhrumilmistry@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: mtk_drm_crtc: do not pass a double to printk

MSYNC_MIN_FPS is a floating point constant (46.1). Kernel code is built
with -mgeneral-regs-only, and newer clang releases reject passing a
double through varargs ("requires 'double' type support"). Print the
constant as a string instead; behaviour is unchanged.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_crtc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_crtc.c
@@ -8014,7 +8014,8 @@
 		fps = drm_mode_vrefresh(mode);
 		time_diff = msync_dy->record[msync_dy->record_index].time -
 			msync_dy->record[last_msync_idx].time;
-		DDPDBG("[Msync] min fps:%f, fps:%d, time_diff:%d\n", MSYNC_MIN_FPS, fps, time_diff);
+		DDPDBG("[Msync] min fps:" __stringify(MSYNC_MIN_FPS) ", fps:%d, time_diff:%d\n",
+			fps, time_diff);
 		if (1000 * 1000 * 1000 / MSYNC_MIN_FPS < time_diff) {
 			msync_dy->record[msync_dy->record_index].low_frame = true;
 			DDPDBG("[Msync] low_frame = true\n");
